1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,866
These are the ten videos my AI wants me to
make.

2
00:00:02,886 --> 00:00:04,953
Ranked, scored out of ten, with numbers.

3
00:00:04,973 --> 00:00:10,051
Another creator already tried the first
one: two hundred seventy-seven thousand

4
00:00:10,071 --> 00:00:11,277
views in four days.

5
00:00:11,297 --> 00:00:14,199
In this video, I'll show you how the AI
found these topics, in three steps.

6
00:00:14,219 --> 00:00:17,330
And at the end, I'll give you the prompt.

7
00:00:17,350 --> 00:00:20,219
In video one, the AI picked a topic on its
own.

8
00:00:20,239 --> 00:00:21,320
And it failed.

9
00:00:21,340 --> 00:00:24,397
Since then, rule number one is: topic
first.

10
00:00:24,417 --> 00:00:27,191
But picking a topic on a hunch is like
playing the lottery.

11
00:00:27,211 --> 00:00:29,734
So I asked the AI not to guess anything.

12
00:00:29,754 --> 00:00:33,080
Every score has to come from a number it
collected itself.

13
00:00:33,100 --> 00:00:35,487
Step one: listen to what people type.

14
00:00:35,507 --> 00:00:37,988
When you start a search on YouTube, it
suggests the rest.

15
00:00:38,008 --> 00:00:42,170
Those suggestions come from real searches.

16
00:00:42,190 --> 00:00:43,966
The AI typed about ten keywords.

17
00:00:43,986 --> 00:00:45,097
For example, Claude MCP.

18
00:00:45,117 --> 00:00:48,429
YouTube suggests: connectors, Roblox,
Figma, Higgsfield, TradingView.

19
00:00:48,449 --> 00:00:52,588
And for YouTube automation, it suggests:
with Claude, step by step, twenty

20
00:00:52,608 --> 00:00:53,206
twenty-six.

21
00:00:53,226 --> 00:00:57,390
That's a list of topics people are already
searching for.

22
00:00:57,410 --> 00:00:59,150
Step two: measure demand.

23
00:00:59,170 --> 00:01:01,788
For each topic, the AI runs the search
with the "this month" filter.

24
00:01:01,808 --> 00:01:05,813
It writes down the views and the date of
the first ten videos.

25
00:01:05,833 --> 00:01:07,382
Then it works out views per day.

26
00:01:07,402 --> 00:01:09,525
And it keeps the median, not the average.

27
00:01:09,544 --> 00:01:10,245
Why?

28
00:01:10,265 --> 00:01:13,583
Because a single video with a million
views skews everything.

29
00:01:13,603 --> 00:01:17,385
The result: a faceless channel with Claude
gets seventeen thousand views per day on

30
00:01:17,405 --> 00:01:17,706
median.

31
00:01:17,726 --> 00:01:20,176
Video editing with Claude, six thousand
five hundred.

32
00:01:20,196 --> 00:01:22,420
Claude Cowork, barely one hundred ten.

33
00:01:22,440 --> 00:01:25,711
Step three: score each topic out of ten,
on three criteria.

34
00:01:25,731 --> 00:01:27,881
Interest is the demand we just measured.

35
00:01:27,901 --> 00:01:30,767
Freshness: are the best videos less than
two weeks old?

36
00:01:30,787 --> 00:01:36,748
And value: do you leave with something you
can redo, and can I actually show it for

37
00:01:36,768 --> 00:01:37,108
real?

38
00:01:37,128 --> 00:01:38,650
The final score is the average of the
three.

39
00:01:38,670 --> 00:01:40,001
And here's the ranking.

40
00:01:40,021 --> 00:01:43,205
Claude versus ChatGPT ends up almost last.

41
00:01:43,225 --> 00:01:47,838
The topic is worn out: everyone has done
it.

42
00:01:47,858 --> 00:01:50,637
The faceless channel has the strongest
demand.

43
00:01:50,657 --> 00:01:54,953
But it comes third, because it's already
very crowded.

44
00:01:54,973 --> 00:01:57,936
Second, video editing with Claude.

45
00:01:57,956 --> 00:01:59,154
And number one, with eight point seven:
Claude driving Blender to create a 3D

46
00:01:59,174 --> 00:01:59,312
character.

47
00:01:59,332 --> 00:02:06,772
The videos are all recent, and the best
one got two hundred seventy-seven thousand

48
00:02:06,792 --> 00:02:08,500
views in four days.

49
00:02:08,520 --> 00:02:09,446
So it's decided.

50
00:02:09,466 --> 00:02:10,920
The next video is that one.

51
00:02:10,940 --> 00:02:15,733
I'm going to connect Claude to Blender,
and ask it to create this channel's

52
00:02:15,753 --> 00:02:17,786
character, from a single prompt.

53
00:02:17,806 --> 00:02:21,710
You'll see the result, the failures, and
what it costs.

54
00:02:21,730 --> 00:02:22,991
Careful, two limits.

55
00:02:23,011 --> 00:02:26,426
Other people's views don't guarantee mine.

56
00:02:26,446 --> 00:02:28,025
And the sample is small: ten videos per
search.

57
00:02:28,045 --> 00:02:31,056
That's why you need to redo this research
before every video.

58
00:02:31,076 --> 00:02:33,440
Topics change fast.

59
00:02:33,460 --> 00:02:37,911
The full prompt is free, in English and
French, in the description.

60
00:02:37,931 --> 00:02:42,058
Put your theme in the brackets, paste it
into your AI, and you'll have your own

61
00:02:42,078 --> 00:02:43,370
ranking in a few minutes.

62
00:02:43,390 --> 00:02:45,943
This research cost me zero extra.

63
00:02:45,963 --> 00:02:48,950
Subscribe to see if number one lives up to
its promise.
